(   [Problem Statement]: Explain JavaScript Closures in depth: definition, lexical scoping, memory retention, and practical use cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   A Closure is the combination of a function bundled together with references to its surrounding) Tj
T*
(   lexical environment \(lexical state\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   In JavaScript, inner functions have access to variables declared in their outer enclosing) Tj
T*
(   functions. A closure gives an inner function access to an outer function's scope even AFTER the) Tj
T*
(   outer function has returned and exited the call stack:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   function createCounter\(\) {) Tj
T*
(   let count = 0; // Private encapsulated variable) Tj
T*
(   return {) Tj
T*
(   increment: function\(\) { count++; return count; },) Tj
T*
(   decrement: function\(\) { count--; return count; },) Tj
T*
(   getValue: function\(\) { return count; }) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   const counter = createCounter\(\);) Tj
T*
(   console.log\(counter.increment\(\)\); // 1) Tj
T*
(   console.log\(counter.increment\(\)\); // 2) Tj
T*
(   console.log\(counter.count\); // undefined \(cannot be accessed directly!\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
