(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Prototypal Inheritance in JavaScript, explaining the prototype chain, Object.prototype, and constructor functions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike class-based languages \(Java, C++\) that instantiate objects from static blueprint) Tj
T*
(   classes, JavaScript uses Prototypal Inheritance, where objects inherit directly from other) Tj
T*
(   objects:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Mechanics of Prototypes:) Tj
T*
(   1. Every function in JavaScript possesses a `prototype` object property.) Tj
T*
(   2. When an object is instantiated with `new Constructor\(\)`, the engine links the object's) Tj
T*
(   internal `[[Prototype]]` \(accessible via `Object.getPrototypeOf\(\)` or `__proto__`\) to) Tj
T*
(   `Constructor.prototype`.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Prototype Chain: When accessing `obj.property`, the engine checks `obj` itself. If not) Tj
T*
(   found, it traverses up to `obj.__proto__`, then `obj.__proto__.__proto__`, until it reaches) Tj
T*
(   `Object.prototype.__proto__`, which is `null`. If still not found, it returns `undefined`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Code Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   function Vehicle\(brand\) {) Tj
T*
(   this.brand = brand;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   Vehicle.prototype.drive = function\(\) {) Tj
T*
(   return `${this.brand} is moving.`;) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   const car = new Vehicle\('Toyota'\);) Tj
T*
(   console.log\(car.drive\(\)\); // Toyota is moving.) Tj
T*
(   console.log\(car.hasOwnProperty\('drive'\)\); // false \(inherited via prototype chain!\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
