(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the JavaScript Event Loop, Call Stack, Web APIs, Task Queue \(Macrotasks\), and Microtask Queue with a sequence diagram description.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   JavaScript runs on a single-threaded runtime environment. Concurrency is achieved via the Event) Tj
T*
(   Loop architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Components:) Tj
T*
(   1. Call Stack: LIFO stack executing synchronous function frames.) Tj
T*
(   2. Web APIs \(Browser Environment\): Background C++ threads handling timers \(setTimeout\), network) Tj
T*
(   requests \(fetch/XHR\), and DOM events.) Tj
T*
(   3. Microtask Queue: Holds callbacks from Promises \(.then/.catch/.finally\), MutationObserver,) Tj
T*
(   and queueMicrotask\(\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Macrotask \(Task\) Queue: Holds callbacks from setTimeout, setInterval, setImmediate, and I/O) Tj
T*
(   events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Event Loop Cycle Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Execute all synchronous code currently in the Call Stack until it is completely empty.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Check the Microtask Queue. Execute ALL queued microtasks one by one until the Microtask) Tj
T*
(   Queue is completely drained \(if microtasks schedule more microtasks, they run in the same) Tj
T*
(   tick\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Perform browser rendering updates \(requestAnimationFrame and Paint\) if necessary.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Dequeue and execute exactly ONE Macrotask from the Task Queue.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Return to Step 2 immediately.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
