(   array methods:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Method Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   1. forEach\(\): Iterates through array elements executing side-effects. Returns `undefined` \(does) Tj
T*
(   not produce a new array\). Cannot be chained.) Tj
T*
(   2. map\(\): Transforms each element via a callback function, returning a new array of identical) Tj
T*
(   length.) Tj
T*
(   3. filter\(\): Tests each element against a predicate boolean function, returning a new array) Tj
T*
(   containing only elements that return `true`.) Tj
T*
(   4. reduce\(\): Accumulates array elements into a single accumulator value \(number, object, or) Tj
T*
(   array\) from left to right.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Functional Pipeline Example:) Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   const products = [) Tj
T*
