(   [Problem Statement]: Explain JavaScript Module System evolution: CommonJS \(require/module.exports\) vs ES6 Modules \(import/export\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   JavaScript modularization evolved from server-side specifications to native language standards:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. CommonJS \(Node.js Default Legacy\):) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: `const math = require\('./math'\);` and `module.exports = { add };`.) Tj
T*
(   - Loading: Synchronous and dynamic \(can be conditionally called inside `if` statements\).) Tj
T*
(   - Output: Copies values at export time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. ES6 Modules \(ESM - Modern Standard\):) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: `import { add } from './math.js';` and `export const add = ...;`.) Tj
T*
(   - Loading: Asynchronous and static. Imports are evaluated at parse-time before execution,) Tj
T*
(   enabling Tree Shaking \(dead code elimination by bundlers\).) Tj
T*
ET

