(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the performance characteristics of V8 JavaScript Engine: Ignition Bytecode Interpreter and TurboFan Optimizing Compiler.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Google's V8 engine executes JavaScript at blazing speed via a multi-tiered JIT compiler) Tj
T*
(   architecture:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The V8 Pipeline:) Tj
T*
(   1. Parser & AST: Source code is parsed into an Abstract Syntax Tree \(AST\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Ignition Interpreter: Ignition rapidly compiles the AST into concise bytecode and begins) Tj
T*
(   execution instantly without startup latency, gathering runtime type feedback.) Tj
T*
(   3. TurboFan JIT Compiler: Hot functions \(frequently executed loops\) with consistent argument) Tj
T*
(   types are passed to TurboFan, which generates ultra-optimized native machine code.) Tj
T*
(   4. Deoptimization \(Bailing Out\): If a hot function optimized for integers suddenly receives a) Tj
T*
(   string argument, TurboFan deoptimizes the native code immediately, falling back to Ignition) Tj
T*
(   bytecode.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

